13. Commit verified changes.
14. Push to an authorized working branch.
15. Report the actual Git SHA and execution results.
16. Release or renew its lease appropriately.

### Important execution requirements

Prevent duplicate claims.

Prevent concurrent ownership after lease expiration.

Ensure stale workers cannot commit results after ownership has been revoked.

Use idempotent operations wherever practical.

